# fritz-wifi password file - one TR-064 login per device.
#
#   host_or_ip   user   password (the rest of the line)
#
# The first field is the hosts.cfg name or the IP address of the device
# (the name is looked up first). "-" as user means the default "xymon";
# the FRITZ!Powerline 1260E ignores the user name, other devices may not.
# The password may contain blanks and any character; blanks at its start
# and end are removed. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Two layouts are accepted, anything else is rejected. Either the file
# belongs to the user running the collector (xymon) and nobody else may
# access it:
#   install -o xymon -g xymon -m 600 /usr/share/doc/my-xymon-extensions-server/fritz-wifi/fritz.passwd.example /etc/xymon/my-xymon-extensions-server/fritz.passwd
# or it belongs to root and only the collector's primary group may read
# it (the collector then cannot change it):
#   install -o root -g xymon -m 640 /usr/share/doc/my-xymon-extensions-server/fritz-wifi/fritz.passwd.example /etc/xymon/my-xymon-extensions-server/fritz.passwd
#
# Examples - copy a line, remove the leading "#" and fill in your values:
#powerline3.lan   -       my password here
#192.168.5.7      xymon   another_password
